;;; A rule whose `:match` is `()` never fires — M1f **W31**, register row
;;; `W31/empty-match-fact` (`corpus/wrong_answers.toml`), banked by S1f.5.0
;;; (2026-11-08) from S1f.5.9's case (P1f.5's F12), filed `open` and owned by
;;; S1f.5.9, on the user's ruling of 2026-11-07 on F12.
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; One fact `(q a)` and a rule with no premise that concludes `(q b)`.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; An empty conjunction is true, so the rule fires once (F12's ruling): root
;;; holds `(q b :rule r)` beside `(q a)`, and R's minimal line is root's state,
;;; `(model (q a) (q b))`.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answers ────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The rule loads and never fires (`ein saturate FILE --dump`): root holds
;;; `(q a)` alone, `(q b)` is a candidate, and R is eight states, exit 0 (`ein
;;; solve FILE` and `ein oracle FILE` at `ec004a48`, the engine `916d97ac`'s,
;;; release and debug alike).
;;;
;;; ── Since M1f S1f.5.9 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `:match ()` is the empty conjunction since T1f.5.9.2 (2026-11-09), so `r`
;;; fires once at root: root holds `(q b :rule r)` beside `(q a)`, H is `(p
;;; a)` and `(p b)`, and R their cube, its minimal line root's state, the
;;; answer above by hand. The register's `now` is that answer; the section
;;; above is the record of the one it replaced.

(relation q Node) (relation p Node)
(q a)
(rule r () :match () :assert (q b))
